```css
.glass {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, #2a1a20 55%, transparent);
  backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(160%);
  border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #fff1f2 18%, transparent);
  border-radius: 18px;
  padding: 2rem;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.35);
}
```

**Why it works:** `backdrop-filter: blur()` blurs whatever is painted *behind* the element — the card itself stays semi-transparent through `color-mix(... transparent)`, so the blurred backdrop shows through. `saturate(160%)` keeps colors vivid behind the frost, and the 1px translucent border simulates the light edge real glass catches.

