```js
const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
  for (const e of entries) {
    if (e.isIntersecting) {
      e.target.classList.add('visible');
      io.unobserve(e.target); // reveal once
    }
  }
}, { threshold: 0.15 });

document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el => io.observe(el));
```

**Why it works:** `IntersectionObserver` fires off the main thread whenever an element's visibility crosses the threshold — far cheaper than scroll listeners computing `getBoundingClientRect()` on every frame. Elements start invisible via CSS, get the `.visible` class once seen, and are unobserved to free memory. The reduced-motion query respects user preferences.

