async functions always return a promise; await pauses the function (not the page) until it settles. Always pair awaits with try/catch or .catch — a rejected promise without handling becomes an unhandled rejection.

```js
async function load() {
  try {
    const res = await fetch("/api/items");
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(res.status);
    return await res.json();
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("load failed:", err);
    return [];
  }
}
```

