A debounced function delays execution until input stops for N ms by resetting a timer on every call — ideal for search inputs and resize handlers that must not fire per keystroke.

```js
function debounce(fn, ms = 300) {
  let t;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(t);
    t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), ms);
  };
}
```

