Same three dots, two directions: in calls/arrays/objects spread expands elements; in function parameters or destructuring rest collects them into an array/object.

```css
const nums = [3, 1, 2];
const sorted = [...nums].sort();          // spread
function sum(...values) { return values.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0); }
```

A debounced function delays execution until input stops for N ms by resetting a timer on every call — ideal for search inputs and resize handlers that must not fire per keystroke.

```css
function debounce(fn, ms = 300) {
  let t;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(t);
    t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), ms);
  };
}
```

